INT. CUBICLE FARM - MONDAY MORNING

Gray partitions. Motivational posters. A potted plant dying on a filing cabinet.

SHANICE, thirties, a headset on, taps a keyboard. COLETTE, forties, her supervisor, stands at the cubicle entrance with a coffee. BARRY, fifties, from HR, hovers behind with a binder.

COLETTE
(to the whole floor)
Team meeting, five minutes, conference B.

Heads pop up above partitions. A groan.

SHANICE
(muttering)
Another meeting.

COLETTE
She heard that.

BARRY
She definitely heard that.

Shanice pulls off her headset. Colette leans against the partition.

COLETTE
Shanice, a word.

SHANICE
Sure.

COLETTE
You've been here seven years.

SHANICE
Eight.

COLETTE
Eight. And we've decided to restructure.

Barry opens his binder. Shanice stares at it.

SHANICE
Restructure.

BARRY
Position eliminated, effective today.

SHANICE
(to the floor, loudly)
They just fired me!

Silence. Every head disappears behind the partitions.
